  "articleBody": "Painting your garage can seem like a simple DIY project, but there are some common pitfalls that can lead to a less-than-stellar result. Knowing these can help you avoid them!\n\n*   **Painting over dirty surfaces:** Garages get dusty and greasy. If you paint over that grime, your new paint won't stick and will likely peel quickly. Always clean and degrease thoroughly first.\n*   **Skipping primer on bare wood or repairs:** Bare drywall, new wood trim, or repaired spots will soak up paint differently, leading to an uneven finish. Primer creates a uniform surface for the topcoat.\n*   **Using interior-grade paint everywhere:** While fine for some parts, garage walls and especially trim often need more durable paint that can withstand impacts, moisture, and temperature fluctuations better than standard interior paint.\n*   **Not protecting adjacent surfaces:** Overspray and drips happen! Failing to properly tape off and cover floors, outlets, or shelving can lead to a messy cleanup. Always take the time to protect what you don't want painted.\n*   **Ignoring existing trim damage:** Painting over rotted, water-damaged, or heavily caulked trim won't fix the underlying issue and will likely look bad quickly. Addressing these repairs beforehand is crucial. \n\nIf you're unsure about any of these steps, especially with extensive damage or prep, calling a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of headache and ensure a great, lasting finish for your Denver-area garage.",
